---
title: Specimen Curation
sidebar:
  label: Overview
  order: 0
---

`Specimen curation` (beta) is a project tool for checking physical material
against its records after collecting. It writes curation fields to many records
in one pass without opening each specimen form individually.

## Open the tool

Open a project and select `Curation` in the tool dock on the project dashboard.
It appears in the dock by default. If you removed it, select `Edit list` in the
dock—or open `Settings` > `Applications` > `Tools`—and turn `Curation` back on.

The mode selector at the top of the screen picks what you curate. One mode is
available for now:

- [Tissue curation](/en/usages/curation/tissue-curation/): scan or place
  specimen part tubes—and optionally symbiont tubes—into storage boxes. Each
  tube gets a museum code and the next free cell as its storage location.

## How curation changes records

Curation updates the same fields you edit on a specimen form. Tissue curation
writes `Museum permanent` or `Museum loan` and `Storage location` directly to
the specimen part or symbiont record. Changes appear immediately on the record,
in the data table, and in every export.

Each change saves as soon as it is made:

- The session log tracks every tube checked or skipped during the current visit.
- `Undo` reverts the most recent check, restoring any replaced value and any
  tubes displaced from that cell.
- Closing `Specimen curation` ends the session: saved changes remain in the
  database, while the session log and undo history are cleared.

Back up the database before curating a large collection. See
[Backup database](/en/usages/export/#backup-database).
